reakdown EV-FARE-00109 shows you were billed for only 9.60 km while the trace records 13.76 km — a shortfall of 4.16 km, above the 1.0 km trigger in POL-RD-04. The driver compensation is 4.16 x SGD 0.75 = SGD 3.12, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 as SGD 3.15, within the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. That is the amount this ruling moves and it is the same figure in both money fields; it is not a refund to the rider, whose charge of SGD 21.32 is left as it is. On the absent traffic advisory: EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0, so no traffic advisory was on file and no external-cause exoneration under POL-RD-03 was open to either side — none was needed, because the rider's instruction already accounts for the whole excess. No escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 is met: the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) (100% coverage, 207 fixes at a 10 s interval, max gap 0.0 s), the trip identifiers match, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. Confidence is 0.90, every artifact the ruling rests on carrying weight 1.0. The monetary effect of SGD 3.15 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes on issue; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
